 "result_text": "I fixed both problems in `pythonfmu/fmi2slave.py`. I haven't run anything, including a build of an FMU or a check against `fmpy`'s validator.\n\n- **Float error:** `startTime`, `stopTime` and `tolerance` are now converted with `str()` before they go into the XML. You can pass plain floats to `DefaultExperiment` and no longer need the `str(0.)` workaround.\n- **Validator error:** `DefaultExperiment` was being written at the end of the file, after `ModelStructure`. The FMI 2 schema requires it before `ModelVariables`, which is why `fmpy` said the element was \"not expected\". It is now written right after `LogCategories` and before `ModelVariables`.\n\nSo it was a bug on the PythonFMU side, not a problem in `fmpy`'s validation.",
